# the twelve A-O distances of a GdFeO3-type perovskite span roughly 2.4-3.2 A,
# and an internal gap can exceed the gap at the boundary. The cut then
# amputates the shell, and because bond valence sums over the shell, the result
# is a spuriously LOW BVS indistinguishable from genuine underbonding.
#
# Measured on 934 ICSD perovskites: 330 sites (322 structures) had cn below
# cn_relative and 472 below geo_cn, with a median BVS deviation of -10.4%
# against -1.4% elsewhere, and 43% of the structures with GII > 0.20 contained
